<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-SWITZERLAND'S KERNEN WINS MEN'S DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SWITZERLAND'S KERNEN WINS MEN'S DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bruno Kernen of Switzerland won the men's downhill gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships on Saturday in a time of one minute 51.11 seconds, according to unofficial results.  </p>
<p>Lasse Kjus of Norway won the silver medal in 1:51.18 and Kristian Ghedina of Italy took bronze in 1:51.46</p>
</text>
